  "body": "### Summary\nAs an app user, I want short, clear and honest survey questions, so that I can give useful feedback in under seven minutes.\n\n### Scope\n- Final wording of every question and answer of `docs/ux/tri-m5-decisions.md` §4: profile questions, opening question, theme 1 (long-topic reading, two scenarios), theme 2 (iPad and Duo: sidebar card sort, three layouts), ten reaction cards, the private-messages question, free field.\n- Three-line introduction, end message, the announcement for the HFR topic and the TestFlight note.\n- Each question linked to its section of the triage document.\n- Rules: user's point of view, no jargon, no promise; an \"as today\" answer wherever relevant.\n\n### Deliverable\n`docs/ux/questionnaire/questions.md` (French).\n\n### Model and review\nSonnet author, Opus review, PO validation. Brief: `docs/ux/cadrage-agents-questionnaire.md` §3, UX-05.\n\nTracked on #628.\n\n### Before you start\n\nRead, in order: `AGENTS.md`, `docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md`, `docs/agents/LESSONS.md`, then `docs/ux/README.md`. The UX documents are in French. Until the docs PR is merged into `dev-swift`, read them on branch `docs/ux-questionnaire`.\n\nRules: no proposal the PO classed **Non** may appear in the survey (`docs/ux/tri-m5-decisions.md` §3.5 and §4.7). The reader keeps the WebView: the survey only shows improvements possible with it. Stop and report if an instruction contradicts the plan.\n\n---\n_Opened with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) for the PO (Bruno), 2026-11-07._\n\n",
